I'll implement three buttons: Start (disabled when running), Pause (disabled when paused), Reset. Or better Start and Pause combined group with active highlight, Reset separate. The explicit separate buttons satisfy.

Let's consider UX: When paused after partial progress, Start resumes. Pause only meaningful while running. Disabled states make it obvious. Add `disabled` with styles.

Implementation: add `start` and `pause` handlers instead of toggle? Can reuse toggle: start sets running true only if not running; pause sets false only if running. Create `startTimer` and `pauseTimer` useCallbacks:

